notes.body:
When a response is saved, the route calls `sendToPipeline` in `apps/web/app/lib/pipelines.ts`, which POSTs to an internal `/api/pipeline` route. That route fans the event out to webhooks, integrations, emails, survey auto-completion and billing. Everything downstream depends on these two requests, so check whether anything queues, awaits or retries them.

Read `pipelines.ts` and answer: what happens before the `fetch`, and which failures does its `.catch` cover? Then open the v1 client responses route and see how `sendToPipeline` is called.

Then read the internal pipeline route, `apps/web/app/api/(internal)/pipeline/route.ts`, top to bottom:

- how webhooks are selected for an event (read the Prisma `where`);
- which headers each delivery gets, and under which condition;
- `fetchWithTimeout` and the comments above it;
- what the promise chain does with a resolved response versus a thrown error (look up when `fetch` rejects);
- the auto-complete block for finished responses.
